# Windows Build Environment (MSYS2 UCRT64)

Carcer uses CMake presets with Ninja. After `scripts/setup-dev.sh`, the normal
developer entry point is the convenience Makefile under `src/`:

- Windows: `.\scripts\Invoke-Ucrt64.ps1 "make -C src"`
- Linux/macOS: `make -C src`

The Makefile delegates to CMake; use explicit presets for qualification work.

On Windows, run UCRT64 compiler and bash commands through the repository
wrapper from PowerShell:

```powershell
.\scripts\Invoke-Ucrt64.ps1 "cmake --preset ucrt64-debug"
.\scripts\Invoke-Ucrt64.ps1 "cmake --build --preset ucrt64-debug --target CARCER"
.\scripts\Invoke-Ucrt64.ps1 "./scripts/run-all-tests-ucrt64.sh"
.\scripts\Invoke-Ucrt64.ps1 "./scripts/update-translations.sh"
```

`scripts/Invoke-Ucrt64.ps1` auto-detects common MSYS2 installations. Override
with `MSYS2_ROOT` if needed. Developer setup generates compile commands under
`build/cmake/dev-debug/compile_commands.json`; explicit UCRT64 qualification
uses `build/cmake/ucrt64-debug/compile_commands.json`.
